-- Bottom-water drive: three oil layers of 3x3 cells with a numerical aquifer
-- connected to the bottom faces (K+) of all of layer 3, and a producer in the
-- middle column completed in layer 1 only.  Layer 4 is an inactive gap and
-- layer 5 is inactive apart from the three aquifer cells.
-- The aquifer cells use their own PVT and saturation tables through AQUNUM
-- items 11 and 12: region 2 has a denser, more viscous brine and straight-line
-- water relative permeability.  The reservoir uses region 1 throughout.  The
-- porosity of the first aquifer cell is defaulted, so it takes the grid value.

RUNSPEC

TITLE
COMPOSITIONAL BOTTOM NUMERICAL AQUIFER WITH ITS OWN TABLES

